<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battles of Kawanakajima</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1553">1553</a>–<a href="/years/1564">1564</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battles of Kawanakajima were five battles fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takeda-shingen">Takeda Shingen</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uesugi-kenshin">Uesugi Kenshin</a> from 1553 to 1564 on the plain of Kawanakajima in northern Shinano, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. The fourth, in 1561, was one of the bloodiest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku period</a>, with heavy losses on both sides, but none of the battles was decisive. They became legendary in Japanese literature and art.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battles-of-kawanakajima.jpg" alt="Battles of Kawanakajima" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: after Katsukawa Shuntei (died in 1824) by Hiroshige(1797-1858) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BattleKawanakajima.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
